      "title": "Grains and Nutrition",
      "audio": "https://storage.googleapis.com/pte-magic-question-2018/question_20230310_1678459435371.mp3",
      "sampleAudioTranscript": "The talk mainly discusses the benefits of adding grains to your diet. First, it explains that grains are easy to find in stores and simple to cook, similar to spaghetti. Then, it highlights that whole grains like barley are nutritious and have health advantages, such as potentially lowering cholesterol. Additionally, grain-based salads are convenient since grains don’t wilt like lettuce. For example, barley can be boiled in salted water and used in meals. Overall, the talk emphasized the importance of including grains for better health."
