      "sampleAudioTranscript": "The talk mainly focuses on how language is different from other cognitive skills. The main idea is that language is both universal and incredibly complex. First, everyone normally learns to speak at least one language, unlike skills like math or music, which not everyone masters. Then, it was explained that because language is so common, people might think it’s simple, but actually, it’s one of the most complex abilities humans have. For example, many people can’t carry a tune, but all children learn to speak. Overall, the discussion highlighted the unique universality and complexity of language."
