      "shortId": "RL0300",
      "transcript": "Traffic light Colors red, amber, and green are used to indicate food's nutritional values according to a healthy standard. Different colors represent different food types so that people can determine what to eat and when they need some certain types of nutrient. The responsibility to label food properly on the packages is on the retailers. Thus, consumers can be aware of food with less salt or less fat. This system makes it easier for consumers to make decisions.",
