      "sampleAudioTranscript": "The talk mainly discusses the debate around protecting biodiversity and its impact on poverty and economic growth. The main idea is whether it’s possible to achieve a win-win situation where economic growth reduces poverty without harming wildlife. First, the speaker pointed out that focusing solely on biodiversity might hurt poor people and slow down economic progress. Then, it was explained that this debate is more complex in developing countries because there’s an extra dimension involving the needs of the poor. An example given was the usual conflict in developed countries over drilling for oil in wildlife areas. Overall, the talk highlighted the challenge of balancing growth, poverty, and conservation."
