      "sampleAudioTranscript": "The talk mainly discusses how parents use two languages to raise their children. The main point is that while parents believe speaking different languages helps kids learn better, it can actually confuse them if both parents switch languages for the same topic. First, the speaker mentioned that confusion happens when each parent uses a different language for the same content. Then, it was explained that confusion is avoided if one parent consistently speaks one language and the other sticks to a different one. For example, parents coming from different countries often do this. Overall, the talk highlighted the importance of consistency in language use for children."
