      "sampleAudioTranscript": "The talk mainly discusses the feudal system during the Middle Ages and how kingdoms were governed. First, it explained that the king ruled the kingdom but couldn’t manage everything alone, so he granted land to important people. Then, the speaker talked about how these lands, called duchies, were controlled by dukes who exchanged loyalty and military support for this land. Additionally, the dukes provided taxes to the king, either as money or a share of farm produce. For example, a duke would pledge to fight alongside the king if the kingdom was threatened. Overall, the talk highlighted how land was the key currency in this system."
