      "sampleAudioTranscript": "The talk mainly discusses how the brain develops through experience and interaction. First, it explains that the brain builds basic circuits for simple skills, then more complex circuits form as we grow. Then, it highlights the role of genetics combined with experience, especially the serve-and-return interaction between children and adults, which shapes brain development. Additionally, the speaker points out that emotional well-being affects learning, since stress or anxiety can interfere even if a child is smart. For example, emotional health impacts how well cognitive skills develop. Overall, the talk emphasized the importance of experience and relationships in shaping the brain."
