      "sampleAudioTranscript": "The talk mainly discusses whether advertising actually works and what impact it has on products. The main idea is that while advertisers spend huge amounts of money, the effect of advertising isn’t always easy to measure. First, the discussion points out that advertising helps increase product awareness and brand loyalty rather than just boosting sales directly. Then, it mentions how advertising budgets have fluctuated over the decades due to economic changes, with examples like the 1996 Olympics and elections boosting spending. Overall, the talk highlights the complex role advertising plays in marketing."
