      "sampleAudioTranscript": "The lecture mainly discusses how happiness is linked to social relationships. The main idea is that the frequency and quality of social interactions with friends, family, and others play a big role in how happy people feel. First, it was mentioned that people who have more frequent happy relations tend to feel more satisfied with their social connections. Then, the talk explained that feeling happier actually makes people enjoy their relationships even more, creating a positive cycle. Another important point is the question of whether social activities lead to happiness or if naturally happy people are just more social. For example, the speaker noted that happy people often spend more time with friends and family. In conclusion, the talk emphasized that good social relations are key to happiness."
