      "sampleAudioTranscript": "The talk mainly discusses vitamin D and its role in the body. First, it explains that vitamin D is a group of fat-soluble compounds, with cholecalciferol being the most important one. Then, I heard about how our main source of vitamin D is from skin synthesis after sun exposure, especially UVB rays, rather than from diet since few foods contain it. Additionally, the vitamin needs to be activated through the liver and kidneys before it works. For example, the speaker mentioned that this process is tightly controlled to prevent toxicity. Overall, the talk highlighted the importance of vitamin D in calcium absorption and metabolism."
