      "sampleAudioTranscript": "The talk mainly discusses how the world has changed a lot over the last 20 to 40 years because of globalization. First, it explained that in the past, a simple event like a chicken sneezing in a small village wouldn’t cause global fear, but now, diseases can quickly spread worldwide. Then, the speaker mentioned how a bank failing in North America used to only affect some people locally, but nowadays, it can shake the entire global economy. Moreover, globalization has brought both problems and amazing achievements, like reaching important development goals sooner than expected. For example, the speaker highlighted the success of the Millennium Development Goals. Overall, the talk showed how connected we are and the power of working together."
