      "sampleAudioTranscript": "The talk mainly discusses the importance of preserving the unique smell of historic libraries. First, the speaker explained that this smell plays a key role in how people perceive and connect with the library environment. Then, they mentioned a study by an advertising company showing that, after sight, smell is the next most important sense we use to interact with our surroundings. An example given was the Wren Library at St Paul's Cathedral, where preserving the smell was a top priority. Overall, the talk highlighted how smell is a crucial way we communicate with spaces."
