      "sampleAudioTranscript": "The talk mainly discusses how deliberate practice is essential for achieving high performance in any skill. First, it explains that practice takes a lot of time and requires identifying and fixing problems and mistakes along the way. Then, it points out that solo musicians, like violinists, spend hundreds of hours practicing alone to improve. Another important point is that this applies to other areas too, like studying geometry, where focusing on weaknesses is key. For example, the speaker mentioned that even talented people need about 10 years of practice to reach international recognition. Overall, the talk highlighted the importance of consistent, focused effort."
