      "audio": "https://storage.googleapis.com/pte-magic-question-2018/SPEAKING_RETELL_LECTURE_1723887289082.mp3",
      "sampleAudioTranscript": "The talk mainly discusses the geography and climate of British Columbia. First, it explains that BC is a large province with rugged mountain ranges running north and south along the coast and islands. Then, I heard about how warm western winds from the Pacific Ocean bring moisture, causing heavy rainfall on the mountain slopes. Additionally, the province is covered by vast forests, including towering Douglas firs, which produce a lot of lumber. For example, these trees can grow up to 300 feet tall. Overall, the talk highlighted the unique natural features of British Columbia."
