      "transcript": "The answer is only one. It's science. It's the human curiosity and the ability to discover and invent new things that's made us live longer, better, happier, and it's going to continue. But then, who are these people who were doing this? And these people are called scientists, and what do they do and how do they do this? Often I have people coming in, especially children. I asked them, who are scientists? What do you know about them? And depending on the age, you get a number of different answers. If you ask a teenager, their information about a scientist comes from Big Bang Theory or, you know, and if you ask a little kid, they often have seen these pictures of these completely crazy nerds who go into their little hole and come up with these crazy ideas, who are unfriendly. I mean, these are all interesting myths and ideas. What I hope I can do today is to tell you a few stories about scientists and what they do. I wish I was as articulate as Arzu was and used all the words about creativity, imagination, connectivity, everything that she said about an artist. The truth is, all of them are true about scientists as well.",
