      "shortId": "RL0653",
      "transcript": "Today we are going to talk about the concept of social identity, an essential part of who we are. Social identity refers to how people define themselves based on the groups they belong to, such as age, gender, race, religion, nationality or even region. It's not just about personal traits. It's deeply tied to our sense of belonging in society. There are several key aspects of social identity, including social identity threats, situations where people feel judged or devalued because of their group membership, and how these can affect well being and performance. And there goes safety threats which relate to whether individuals feel psychologically safe in certain environments based on their identity. Why is social identity important and what impact does it have on us? It depends on different societies and different classifications. The influence of social identity isn't fixed. It varies depending on context, culture and individual experiences. In some settings, your identity might empower you. In others, it might make you feel excluded. Ultimately, understanding social identity helps us recognize how group memberships shape our thoughts, behaviors and interactions. It reminds us that identity isn't just personal, it's social dynamic and deeply powerful.",
