      "title": "Food waste in the USA",
      "transcript": "The United States is often regarded as the largest contributor to food waste globally, with approximately 60% of food waste originating from general consumption. This waste is largely attributed to two key sources. The first is supermarkets, where a significant portion of food waste occurs, particularly in the use-by or expiry date sections. Items that are near or past their expiration date are often discarded, even though they may still be safe for consumption. The second contributing factor lies in consumer purchasing and eating habits. People frequently buy more food than they need or fail to use leftovers, resulting in unnecessary waste. To address this issue, it’s crucial to raise awareness about mindful purchasing and proper food consumption. Encouraging individuals to buy only what they can realistically use and avoid overbuying. This could significantly reduce food waste and help make a positive impact on the environment.",
