      "transcript": "So, you've been asked to write a business plan as part of your next assignment. But what is the purpose of a business plan and why is it so essential? According to recent studies, more millennials, such as you guys in the room, are becoming entrepreneurial and launching their own start-ups. Yet, the same studies show that often, some of these companies have never actually composed a business plan, and only consider it if they require financing. So, let's discuss if business plans are still as crucial as they once were. To obtain backing from a potential investor or venture capitalist, a plan needs to be designed, one that has carefully considered the financial risks for all parties involved – this is the main purpose of your plan – to reassure your prospective financial backer. You may require a backer or a cash injection for numerous reasons.  According to research, the most common reasons are to raise money for stock, to grow the company by buying up smaller competitors, for clearing debt or for equity finance. Regardless of the motive, ensure your plan for your business is clear, credible and goes into enough detail to entice an investor, while still showing that their capital is secure in your hands. Your research that has gone into the plan should provide sound answers and should show that you have made assessments and forecasts for the upcoming business year.",
