      "shortId": "SST0363",
      "title": "SST0363",
      "transcript": "Now, let's look at the eating habits of common garden birds. A recent study has shown that the best way of teaching one particular type of garden bird, the blue tit, how to avoid food which tastes disgusting or could be dangerous, is to play them videos of a different species of tit eating. When the blue tits saw this other species eating and rejecting food, they quickly learned from what they saw and didn't eat that type of food themselves. This gave the blue tits an obvious advantage. It meant that they didn't have to spend so much time and energy trying different types of food in order to find the ones they could eat without harming themselves. Another benefit was that they were less likely to become ill after eating food that's bad for them.",
