      "transcript": "The term innovation is at risk of becoming a buzzword. Popular blogger James Harper has suggested that the word itself is problematic, as it is used to cover too many different aspects of a complex range of ideas. He has recommended breaking down the concept of innovation into types not completely new or distinct types, but just subcategories of the idea of how to innovate. Chief among those is the association of innovation with process strategy and management technique. At the same time, though, the idea has also been strongly linked to the more abstract concept of creativity, a term that's just as hard to pin down. Experts generally concur that innovation done well leads to increased job opportunities, profit, and better standards of living, but it will be hard to develop strategies to encourage these things.",
